You're not fully unpacking the source. People are trying to help you, 
but you need to follow the instructions they give you. You can't take 
shortcuts and then complain that it doesn't work.

Now, I don't use tar and gzip myself; I use winzip. Here's how it works 
for me: I open nethack-343-src.gz with winzip. A popup dialog box tells 
me, "Please enter the full name of the file contained within the archive 
nethack-343-src.gz".

I type in "nethack-343-src.tar". The ".tar" is important--it tells 
winzip that the opened file is still compressed. When I hit "enter," it 
says, "Archive contains one file: nethack-343-src.tar. Should winzip 
decompress it to a temporary folder and open it?"

I choose "yes". And all of a sudden, winzip displays all the files that 
are in the source.

I select all of them, and extract them into the folder that I want my 
nethack source to be in.

Once you've done that, you'll find the folders and files we've been 
talking about. The source isn't just one file; it's a bunch of files all 
organized within several folders.

